<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait bank assets rise in December month/month.</title>
<headline>Kuwait bank assets rise in December month/month.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Combined assets of banks operating in Kuwait rose to 11.458 billion dinars at the end of December from 11.423 billion at the end of November, a Central Bank monthly bulletin said.</p>
<p>Assets were 11.592 billion dinars in December 1995.</p>
<p>Figures in million Kuwaiti dinars</p>
<p>					    December '96   December'95</p>
<p> Cash					  61.4		104.1</p>
<p> Balances with Central Bank	    61.6		 54.0</p>
<p> Public debt instruments	    1,728.4	    1,997.6</p>
<p> Debt purchase bonds		  2,845.0	    3,393.8</p>
<p> Other local investments		327.9		368.9</p>
<p> Credit facilities to</p>
<p>  residents			     3,173.1	    2,436.3</p>
<p> Foreign assets			 2,168.2	    2,130.8</p>
<p> Inter bank local deposits	    662.5		577.1</p>
<p> Other assets			     429.9		529.4</p>
<p> Total				   11,458.1	   11,592.1</p>
<p>Note: Data covers eight commercial and specialised banks,Islamic finance institution Kuwait Finance House and Kuwait's branch of a Bahrain-based bank.</p>
<p>Debt purchase bonds include the value of the purchase by the government of the real estate portfolio of Kuwait Finance House in December 1991.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in totals are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.303 dinar)</p>
<p>Kuwait newsroom, Inal Ersan +965-243-1920</p>
